{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D2Eexym55xHmB4qzx5rKfJ","type":"tool_result","content":"catalog-info.yaml:6:# - Dependencies: S3 bucket, herd-device-api (customer lookup, used by the processor).\n.github/workflows/alert_pr_approved.yaml:3:# Same pattern as herd-device-api (one of the alert_pr_* workflows).\n.github/workflows/pr-review.yaml:3:# Same pattern as herd-device-api. Runs an automated review on each PR and posts\n.github/workflows/alert_pr_new.yaml:3:# Same pattern as herd-device-api (one of the alert_pr_* workflows).\ndocs/grafana/README.md:3:Will hold the dashboard for the upload service as a JSON export, as herd-device-api does (design doc p.37).\nupload-service/openapi.yaml:6:# Open: herd-device-api keeps its spec at api/openapi.yaml; confirm with the team whether to\ndocs/architecture/decisions/0019-customer-from-herd-device-api.md:1:# 0019: Customer from herd-device-api\ndocs/architecture/decisions/0019-customer-from-herd-device-api.md:11:The processor looks up the customer by MAC in herd-device-api through its Cloud8 SDK, with a 15-minute cache so a short outage is mostly absorbed. The MAC to customer endpoint still needs confirming in its api/openapi.yaml, so the POC uses a stub that answers \"unassigned\". SMP was the other option.\ndocs/architecture/decisions/README.md:22:0017 to 0024: the processor and its DynamoDB index. S3 events straight to SQS, one HeadObject per object, the customer from herd-device-api, unknown MACs as \"unassigned\", create-only rows, the customer index, the configuration defaults, and keys that do not parse failing through redrive (which differs from the design doc). Production configuration values are set per environment later.\nprocessor/src/main/java/com/_8x8/herd/device_logs/processor/customer/package-info.java:2: * Who owns a MAC, behind an interface, so the POC stub can give way to herd-device-api without touching indexing.\nprocessor/src/main/java/com/_8x8/herd/device_logs/processor/customer/UnassignedCustomerLookup.java:8: * The POC stub, no MAC has a customer, so every row is \"unassigned\" until the herd-device-api endpoint is confirmed."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50fba3bc-f113-4cef-8e19-4cdf252c7af6","uuid":"2506fca3-e633-430b-a9d0-2e2f71075d0f","timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:18:18.607Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"catalog-info.yaml:6:# - Dependencies: S3 bucket, herd-device-api (customer lookup, used by the processor).\n.github/workflows/alert_pr_approved.yaml:3:# Same pattern as herd-device-api (one of the alert_pr_* workflows).\n.github/workflows/pr-review.yaml:3:# Same pattern as herd-device-api. Runs an automated review on each PR and posts\n.github/workflows/alert_pr_new.yaml:3:# Same pattern as herd-device-api (one of the alert_pr_* workflows).\ndocs/grafana/README.md:3:Will hold the dashboard for the upload service as a JSON export, as herd-device-api does (design doc p.37).\nupload-service/openapi.yaml:6:# Open: herd-device-api keeps its spec at api/openapi.yaml; confirm with the team whether to\ndocs/architecture/decisions/0019-customer-from-herd-device-api.md:1:# 0019: Customer from herd-device-api\ndocs/architecture/decisions/0019-customer-from-herd-device-api.md:11:The processor looks up the customer by MAC in herd-device-api through its Cloud8 SDK, with a 15-minute cache so a short outage is mostly absorbed. The MAC to customer endpoint still needs confirming in its api/openapi.yaml, so the POC uses a stub that answers \"unassigned\". SMP was the other option.\ndocs/architecture/decisions/README.md:22:0017 to 0024: the processor and its DynamoDB index. S3 events straight to SQS, one HeadObject per object, the customer from herd-device-api, unknown MACs as \"unassigned\", create-only rows, the customer index, the configuration defaults, and keys that do not parse failing through redrive (which differs from the design doc). Production configuration values are